"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KXZV12FG1S0M4XP\",\"title\":\"Project Kalki - Facility 1 — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Project Kalki - Facility 1\",\"Earthrevive Technologies\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"QPT1\",\"Crediting period\",\"08 Aug 2026 to 08 Aug 2036\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"QPT1\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 Sep 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://earthrevive.earth\",\"t\":\"Earthrevive Technologies\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JW84N7721S0PCYD\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JW84N7721S0PCYD/prj_1KXZV12FG1S0M4XP/pjd_1M1EJ80V41S0AY8E/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nProject Kalki - Facility 1\\nEarthrevive Technologies\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nQPT1\\nCrediting period\\n08 Aug 2026 to 08 Aug 2036\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nWe are developing a project with smallholder farmers in India to prevent the open-field burning of agricultural residue by converting it into biochar. The biochar is applied to agricultural soils, where it durably sequesters CO₂ .\\n\\nMaharashtra\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 10 Sep 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n01 Sep 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"